ta \\cdot n \\\\  & =3\\cdot 15\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{40}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =45\\cdot (0.642\\,78…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(28.925\\,44…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈28.9n.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127846/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09aeb7f5-31e0-5b2d-9e2a-8eace54a6665"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127846"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-279284/field-1/880c1f1878e7bf9003954193f103ef1194ccc63523bd2fc70ad80fbf9fbafa81" :answer/id #uuid "3cf6fa1c-dced-5860-8a4b-77a37f5d34a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30.15n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279284/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b73c8626-a41c-5107-b9d1-2153b26b1cfa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279284/field-1/880c1f1878e7bf9003954193f103ef1194ccc63523bd2fc70ad80fbf9fbafa81" :answer-field/choices ["q-279284/field-1/880c1f1878e7bf9003954193f103ef1194ccc63523bd2fc70ad80fbf9fbafa81"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279284" :question/id #uuid "824628c7-1546-5ed3-9b1a-834e6b63983a" :question/math-academy-id "q-279284" :question/problem "Given the vector $a$ has magnitude $11$, the vector $b$ has magnitude $3,$ the angle between $a$ and $b$ is ${66}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $a\\times b.$ Find $a\\times b$ in terms of $n.$ \n\nType $n$ to represent the vector $n$ and round your final answer to **two decimal places** where appropriate.\n\n$a\\times b≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|a|\\cdot |b|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =11\\cdot 3\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{66}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =33\\cdot (0.913\\,54…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(30.146\\,82…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈30.15n.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-279284/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09aeb7f5-31e0-5b2d-9e2a-8eace54a6665"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279284"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-146264"] :question/worked-solution "Suppose $a$ and $b$ are nonzero vectors. Then, $a\\times b=0$ if and only if $a∥b.$\n\nNotice that any vector is parallel to itself. So, we have $a∥a.$\n\nTherefore, $a\\times a=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-146313/selection/d714b998afbac312154d9f7bddde27f766eb1b0bc7289be8fddc462b9621d8e8" :answer/id #uuid "837cc8c0-7088-5897-98eb-4ee896fb4fd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5b" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-146313/selection/103b92f32dd36a3e04b4fcf3b1bd2f942d0d112352738a92fb52ab3b3a7740d4" :answer/id #uuid "96f24f51-90bb-530e-836f-aa97b1f27f5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2b" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-146313/selection/4b0c5771c7f352b6cd3896b44d326763393dd7cc7b4f41fab958b73144c6ca0a" :answer/id #uuid "c7593d58-ed9f-5a48-a225-e51fb65750ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-146313/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "f1d18c1d-7479-5fe1-8f76-1522e3f5a8d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-146313/selection/5e20b724469865c2b63e9e178793efb31dea777c0241ef3a3116cbb2734691c2" :answer/id #uuid "53c56342-a7a4-5dbc-8a65-c464f42cd294" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-146313/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "216d3ce6-ebc4-5061-bd66-d9c69aa8b0ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-146313/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc